00:04:20.633 --> 00:04:21.466
- So the question is,

00:04:21.466 --> 00:04:22.790
how can this be legal?

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:24.610
Well, we start with the extremely

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:27.480
long waiver that participants
are forced to sign.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.490
According to news reports,

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.220
neighbors have called
the police when they hear

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.240
or see something scary
at the McKamey place.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:33.420
But police don't file charges

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.280
because the participants signed a waiver.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.470
A waiver, as you probably know,

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.160
is an agreement that offers a business

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:39.080
two protections.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.750
First, the waiver relieves one party

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:43.320
of any blame or liability
arising from negligence

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.690
or wrong-doing regarding
the particular activity,

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.870
such as running through
a bunker's haunted house.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.570
Second. One party, usually the one

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:50.500
that drafted the agreement,

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.500
is freed from all liability arising

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.370
out of the performance of that contract.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.250
Now, if you've ever
interacted in the real world,

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.150
you know that you can
find liability waivers

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.670
and disclaimers almost anywhere.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.890
Like a dry cleaner receipt
prohibiting the dry cleaner

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:03.900
from liability for damage to the clothing.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.770
Or a normal amusement park

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:07.780
that doesn't torture its patrons,

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.390
you can find a waiver on the ticket.

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:11.470
Or signs such as swim at your own risk

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:12.850
or park at your own risk.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:14.300
From a public policy perspective,

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.610
it's considered positive to let

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:17.300
private parties regulate their own affairs

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.290
and allocate risk.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.210
However the law also won't let parties

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.520
be completely reckless.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.370
Especially when there's
unequal bargaining power.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.630
Since courts have to balance
all of these factors,

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.070
anyone running a recreational

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:28.097
or event based business,

00:05:28.097 --> 00:05:31.060
needs a waiver that satisfies
specific conditions.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.850
So let's talk about
some of those conditions

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.550
which includes that a
waiver must be voluntary.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:36.670
A waiver is a contract

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.150
or an addendum to a contract.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.870
And for that contract to be valid,

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.050
the parties have to demonstrate

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:42.870
that they voluntarily entered into it.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.110
This means that the person entered

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.660
into it freely without
coercion or interference,

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.250
and that the person had the knowledge

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:49.530
and capacity to act.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.870
Now there's no evidence
that McKamey lets minors

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.210
or people with diminished capacity

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:54.340
go through the manner.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:55.370
But the bigger question is

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.100
whether people are voluntarily
signing that waiver.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.700
In Schneckloth versus Bustamonte,

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:00.880
the Supreme court stated that

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.710
a waiver is not valid if quote,

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.068
coerced by explicit or implicit means,

00:06:05.068 --> 00:06:07.950
by implied threat or covert force.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.100
And before McKamey will
agree to take someone

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.390
through this creation,

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.570
they have to sit down with him

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:14.950
and discuss what may happen
during the experience.

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:18.200
Participants are asked to
sign a 30 to 40 page waiver

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.610
limiting McKamey's liability
for anything that happens.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.390
They watch a two hour video showing

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:24.580
